WEBVTT

00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:10.591
Hi there.

00:00:10.591 --> 00:00:11.999
Welcome to this video

00:00:11.999 --> 00:00:15.199
where we are going to learn
about protecting your digital identity.

00:00:15.919 --> 00:00:20.319
Digital identity includes your accounts,
passwords, and online data.

00:00:20.911 --> 00:00:23.919
Protecting it helps keep you safe online.

00:00:29.071 --> 00:00:34.351
Your digital identity includes
usernames, profiles, passwords, and data.

00:00:35.151 --> 00:00:38.879
It also includes your messages, 
photos, and digital footprint

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:42.111
created due to your actions
in the digital environment.

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:45.279
All of these are connected to you online.

00:00:45.279 --> 00:00:47.919
That is why protection is important.

00:00:47.919 --> 00:00:52.319
Digital identity is valuable because it
gives access to accounts and information.

00:00:52.959 --> 00:00:55.951
Attackers may want to steal or misuse it.

00:00:56.271 --> 00:00:59.551
Protecting identity prevents
others from pretending to be you.

00:01:00.111 --> 00:01:03.119
It also protects your reputation.

00:01:03.391 --> 00:01:06.159
There are several risks
to digital identity.

00:01:06.159 --> 00:01:10.799
These include weak passwords,
sharing information, and unsafe behavior.

00:01:11.519 --> 00:01:14.511
Phishing messages
and fake links are also risks.

00:01:15.135 --> 00:01:17.263
Knowing the risks helps you avoid them.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:25.487
Strong passwords
are one of the most important protections.

00:01:25.727 --> 00:01:28.735
They make it harder for attackers
to access accounts.

00:01:29.087 --> 00:01:32.015
Each account
should have its own strong password.

00:01:32.015 --> 00:01:35.007
This limits damage
if one account is attacked.

00:01:35.535 --> 00:01:39.247
Password managers help manage
many strong passwords safely.

00:01:39.327 --> 00:01:42.335
They reduce the need 
to remember many passwords.

00:01:42.687 --> 00:01:45.135
They also prevent password reuse.

00:01:45.135 --> 00:01:48.127
Using them supports good security habits.

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:51.375
Privacy settings control
who can see your information.

00:01:51.887 --> 00:01:54.895
They help limit
how much data others can access.

00:01:55.327 --> 00:01:58.047
Checking settings
regularly is a good habit.

00:01:58.047 --> 00:02:01.055
Settings are powerful protection tools.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:03.775
Logging out
is important on shared devices.

00:02:03.775 --> 00:02:06.735
It stops others 
from opening your accounts.

00:02:06.735 --> 00:02:09.727
Using device locks also protects identity.

00:02:10.095 --> 00:02:12.815
Small actions make a big difference.

00:02:12.815 --> 00:02:16.207
Phishing messages try to trick people
into giving information.

00:02:16.847 --> 00:02:20.575
They may look urgent
or pretend to be trusted sources.

00:02:20.575 --> 00:02:23.567
Stopping and thinking 
helps avoid these tricks.

00:02:24.207 --> 00:02:26.095
When unsure, do not click.

00:02:27.055 --> 00:02:30.815
Sharing too much personal information
can help attackers to collect

00:02:30.815 --> 00:02:34.943
personal details that they can use
to gain access to your digital assets.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:38.703
For example,
by guessing passwords or usernames.

00:02:39.407 --> 00:02:42.446
Think carefully
before posting or sending details.

00:02:42.686 --> 00:02:45.614
Ask yourself who will see it and why.

00:02:45.614 --> 00:02:49.534
Careful sharing can help to protect
your digital identity and assets.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.678
Old and unused accounts
can still store data.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:56.190
Deleting them reduces risk.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.670
A clean digital space is safer.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:01.150
Regular cleanups are helpful.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.142
Trusted adults can help
when something feels wrong.

00:03:04.526 --> 00:03:06.606
Asking for help is a smart choice.

00:03:06.606 --> 00:03:09.326
It can prevent mistakes and problems.

00:03:09.326 --> 00:03:12.334
You do not have to handle issues alone.

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:16.030
Protecting digital identity 
is not one big action.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.830
It is made of small daily habits.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:21.262
Safe choices over time add up.

00:03:21.262 --> 00:03:22.990
Consistency is important.

00:03:27.326 --> 00:03:30.318
Digital identity needs protection.

00:03:31.022 --> 00:03:33.902
Strong passwords, 
managers and careful behavior

00:03:33.902 --> 00:03:37.950
help smart habits
keep accounts and data safe.

00:03:38.862 --> 00:03:41.854
You have control
over your digital identity.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.998
Thank you for watching.

00:03:45.998 --> 00:03:48.958
Do not forget to watch
other videos in our series.